{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared case table for the TURN-endpoint host classification, asserted against ALL THREE",
    "implementations of it so they cannot silently diverge:",
    "  services/dedicated-server/src/turn/public-endpoint.ts  classifyTurnHost  (runtime/doctor)",
    "  infrastructure/install/install-chantivo.sh             host_is_non_public (installer)",
    "  scripts/verify-infrastructure.mjs                      nonPublicTurnHost  (repo guard)",
    "The triplication is deliberate: three different runtimes with no shared module boundary (a",
    "standalone Bash installer that must work from a bare checkout, a TypeScript service, and a",
    "plain-Node repository guard). This file is the single source of truth for what they must agree on.",
    "'nonPublic: true' means a remote client on the internet could never reach that host — it is NOT",
    "a claim that a 'false' host IS reachable; nothing running on the server can determine that."
  ],
